OL,3,AEx-gang boss sentenced to 40 years for
OL,4,Aorchestrating Tupac Shakur's murder
OL,5,
OL,6,FFormer gang boss Duane "Keffe D" Davis
OL,7,Fhas been sentenced to at least 40 years
OL,8,Fin prison for orchestrating the murder
OL,9,Fof Tupac Shakur.
OL,11,FA jury found Davis, 63, guilty in
OL,12,FSeptember of one count of murder with a
OL,13,Fdeadly weapon for the rap superstar's
OL,14,Fdeath in a drive-by shooting in Las
OL,15,FVegas on 7 September 1996. He has said
OL,16,Fhe will appeal the verdict.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG10/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,162,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11911
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1791951491
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AEx-gang boss sentenced to 40 years for
OL,4,Aorchestrating Tupac Shakur's murder
OL,5,
OL,6,FProsecutors argued that although Davis
OL,7,Fdid not fire the gun himself, he was
OL,8,Fthe ringleader of the group that
OL,9,Fcommitted the murder. He admitted in
OL,10,Fhis memoir that he had provided the gun
OL,11,Fused in the crime.
OL,13,FDavis' conviction was the first in a
OL,14,Fcold case that has intrigued hip-hop
OL,15,Ffans for nearly 30 years.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG11/19
